{"authored" [{"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "98134812a30d155c701221a65f5480f7b75f9d6425c5ce2d002b9c4852e14599" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "98134812a30d155c701221a65f5480f7b75f9d6425c5ce2d002b9c4852e14599" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "769f9c3e23fde5efa65243b816f9924113c584fc25b7d3d03ba7cbe9e8104510" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "769f9c3e23fde5efa65243b816f9924113c584fc25b7d3d03ba7cbe9e8104510" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "05e9abb1d54b649d715a2304054673723b731aabb1c8f492f1bfab4f9b2c9b85" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "05e9abb1d54b649d715a2304054673723b731aabb1c8f492f1bfab4f9b2c9b85" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9baffd44875b5a849fdb95dc21f8df6622eeea1f939b9623a8eeea5e94747cc6" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(32-0)+1(0-0)+2(0-0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9baffd44875b5a849fdb95dc21f8df6622eeea1f939b9623a8eeea5e94747cc6" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "categ