y/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\n- $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $S$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(S)=\\sqrt{3}$\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+4)-2(-2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3})+0 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9baffd44875b5a849fdb95dc21f8df6622eeea1f939b9623a8eeea5e94747cc6" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I  only"] "category" "ma_ca