ke/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I  only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9baffd44875b5a849fdb95dc21f8df6622eeea1f939b9623a8eeea5e94747cc6" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.j