er/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc836edc25f709b716f8273b349524e5613e0a1ad540937b464e88a4025696ac" "basis" 1374 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039569/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen