|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(4-0)-0+0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =6|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+7|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-2-0)-0+7(0-2) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-2)+7\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-12-14 \\\\  & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-26"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(32-0)+1(0-0)+2(0-0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-24"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\n- $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $S$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(S)=\\sqrt{3}$\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+4)-2(-2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3})+0 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I  only"] ["text" "I and III  only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I  only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $N$ given below?\n\n- $N$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $N$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(N)=-1$\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|+(-\\frac{1}{7})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(-\\frac{4}{7}+\\frac{5}{7})-3(-\\frac{1}{49}+\\frac{1}{49})-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{5}{7}-\\frac{4}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}-3\\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}-\\frac{1}{49} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(N)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $E$ given below?\n\n- $E$ is a singular matrix\n- $E$ is **not**  a singular matrix\n- $det(E)=-2$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 8\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(40-42)-3(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{12}{3})+4(\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(E)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-38179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\frac{2}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(2-\\frac{3}{2})-\\frac{2}{5}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-77478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-1$ only"] ["text" "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only"] ["text" "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only"] ["text" "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only"] ["text" "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-18256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $22$, find all the possible values of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-5$ and $-3$ only"] ["text" "$-8$ and $-1$ only"] ["text" "$5$ and $3$ only"] ["text" "$7$ only"] ["text" "$8$ and $3$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-130580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$-8$ and $-1$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-6|\\begin{aligned}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+m|\\begin{aligned}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-5$ and $1$ only"] ["text" "$-6$ and $3$ only"] ["text" "$1$ only"] ["text" "$4$ and $8$ only"] ["text" "$8$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-128506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$4$ and $8$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is $32$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(-2\\cdot 0-(-1)(4))-3(x\\cdot 0-(-1)(1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(4)-3(1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-8-3 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-11 & =32 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =43 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{43}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{43}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b53caf9028667059bb96c79b5f089b296a98767a9868c01ac7c0562532ac914"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "q-280540" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/state.json" "file_sha256" "36936811e39af34909d761cd987220e54ce8540161c5c85d3ec4580e10d40d5f"} {"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/8e7935fce161e2a1ed706ec03bb5cd202e8c4650ba01ca5e4633f9f1c121d04a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "a8814a5848fc119373f0cdcc053ec5b566cbc7ed9aed9a6cb990fc6b1c2840c7"} {"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "a8814a5848fc119373f0cdcc053ec5b566cbc7ed9aed9a6cb990fc6b1c2840c7"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/21cd71e00c682ad1117b9ae126adcbeb8e4c55769c73eae1e1169534f2a01d4a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "0f6321e3fed9aa609649aea72f75f3105f9c29e18664ca69a7c778564b2a4e06"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "0f6321e3fed9aa609649aea72f75f3105f9c29e18664ca69a7c778564b2a4e06"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "393b448f8e49211e5223dc2ede5e819737b25a5015727c7e2486bdb457d8ccc4"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "393b448f8e49211e5223dc2ede5e819737b25a5015727c7e2486bdb457d8ccc4"}] "usage" {"q-77477" [] "q-128476" [] "q-128506" [] "q-280390" [] "e-14762" [] "e-14763"